# Licensing of the ctbench RTL corpus

ctbench ships two kinds of material under two different licences.

## 1. The harness — Apache License 2.0

Everything under `ctbench/` other than `ctbench/fixtures/`, plus the tests and
packaging, is licensed under the Apache License 2.0.  See `LICENSE`.

## 2. The RTL fixtures — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International

The Verilog fixtures in `ctbench/fixtures/` are licensed
**CC-BY-4.0** (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), except for the
third-party derivatives listed in section 3.

A benchmark corpus is only useful if people can copy fixtures into papers, slides
and competing tools without friction, so the corpus is deliberately licensed more
permissively than a code licence would allow for prose and figures.  Attribution
is the only condition: cite ctbench when you evaluate on it.

Suggested citation:

    ctbench: a matched-pair constant-time RTL benchmark corpus, version 1.0.0.

